        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: la preuve",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "la preuve — \"the proof, the evidence\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Tu dis que c'est lui, mais tu n'as aucune preuve. You say it was him, but you have no proof."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Faire preuve de — to show a quality: faire preuve de courage."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "preuve is usually traced to Old French prueve, a noun formed on prouver \"to prove\", which is inherited from Latin probāre \"to test, to examine\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
